[h1]Military Drop - Radio Supply Airdrops[/h1]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/BATMAN_EHE_MILITARY_DROP/main/docs/steam/banner.png[/img]

[b]Build 42.21 · Singleplayer & Multiplayer · Standalone[/b]

[i]Built for dedicated servers (the server decides everything), mostly tested in singleplayer so far. Please report any multiplayer issue.[/i]

Tune a military radio to the right frequency, give this week's code and requisition supplies. A helicopter drops a crate far away and announces the grid to everyone listening... and the noise draws the dead.

[h2]How it works[/h2]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/BATMAN_EHE_MILITARY_DROP/main/docs/steam/walkie-logistics.png[/img]

[olist]
[*][b]Find the frequency and the code.[/b] Military and police memos give the frequency; every Monday, decipher the shortwave numbers station with the military codebook.
[*][b]Call from a military radio.[/b] Right-click it, [b]Device Options[/b], [b]Logistics[/b] section: type the code and press [b]Request a supply drop[/b].
[*][b]Fill the requisition form.[/b] 18 lots built from the loot tables (your mods included), within a budget set by your trust. Or a siren decoy to lure hordes away.
[*][b]Reach the crate.[/b] It lands 150 to 400 tiles away, guarded by a horde. Keep a radio on the military frequency: the grid is repeated until a case is opened.
[/olist]

[h2]New: Fulton extraction[/h2]

Send intelligence to the army by balloon. Request a pick-up with [b]Request a Fulton pick-up[/b], put a [b]Fulton recovery kit[/b] on the ground outside, fill it with ID cards, paperwork, stash maps or NBC gear, then [b]Inflate and release the Fulton[/b] with a [b]Helium tank[/b]. An aircraft snatches it and the base pays you in trust. Craft the kit or repair a damaged one found in army storage, wrecks or crates.

[h2]Earn the base's trust[/h2]

Each character has a personal reputation, never shown as a number. It shortens the wait between drops and unlocks bigger requisitions.

[list]
[*]Open your own drop first, send a flight recorder from a wreck.
[*]Daily reports, dog tags of fallen soldiers, recon, clearance orders, radio checks, Fulton shipments.
[*]Lose it when outsiders open your drops or when a drop is lost.
[/list]

[h2]And also[/h2]

[list]
[*][b]Helicopter crashes[/b], more frequent in storms: a MAYDAY gives the sector; the wreck holds parts, documents and a flight recorder.
[*][b]Liaison post[/b]: a fixed military radio becomes your station's console (tasks, orders, log, recorder bay).
[*][b]Contested drop zones[/b] for PvP servers, drawn in game by the admin.
[*]60 sandbox options, applied without restarting; server-authoritative multiplayer; admin tools from a military radio.
[/list]

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]

[list]
[*]No other mod required.
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3817018338][b]Belt Walkie-Talkie[/b][/url] (optional) is recommended: one shared belt walkie-talkie behaviour for all the mods that use it. Without it, the same behaviour is built in.
[*]Designed to coexist with [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3672792485]HEF - Helicopter Event Framework[/url].
[*]With [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3811010882]Signal Smoke[/url], green smoke marks the crate.
[*]With [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3615135168]Zombie Virus Vaccine[/url], samples and vaccines can be sent by Fulton.
[*]Better Walkie Talkies is supported; items from your mods appear in the crates.
[/list]

